 "open_questions": [
  "WHICH BTC BAR SERIES IS THE REGISTERED OBJECTIVE \u2014 the repo fixture or Hyperliquid's own candles? Over the IDENTICAL window the donchian leg is +0.20 ann.SR / 59 trades on the fixture and -0.78 / 28 trades on HL, and the diversification multiple is 1.25x vs 1.66x. The book EXECUTES on HL, which argues HL's prints are the execution-correct basis, but every published number in the repo rests on the fixture. This is a dated protocol amendment Casey signs, not something I can resolve, and it moves the answer by a third.",
  "IS THERE ANY LONGER OR OUT-OF-SAMPLE ETH HISTORY? Hyperliquid serves only 5,000 candles (2.19y) and ETH is the single asset carrying this entire candidate. Its 1.45 ann.SR fails family-wise multiple testing on that window (p=0.275). Pulling ETH bars from another venue would re-open the data-basis problem above rather than settle it. Without an independent window I cannot distinguish ETH's edge from the best of twelve tries, and I will not size on it. This is the single decisive missing input.",
  "IS A 6x INCREASE IN LIVE-MONEY SURFACE AREA ACCEPTABLE? mirror.py's sizing rails (_leg_frac, _base, _cap_room, _leg_qty, _check_exposure, _check_kelly_cap) are scalar single-asset throughout, and cap_room is consumed SEQUENTIALLY across legs. barbell-lab check_slippage freezes ONE set of slip norms from the first 10 fills; BTC spread is 0.12bp and SOL's is 8.3bp, so a single CUSUM across 6 assets is meaningless. This is a rails rewrite on the live path, not a config change.",
  "IS CASEY ADDING CAPITAL, AND ON WHAT TRAJECTORY? Unchanged from phase 1 and still decisive: even the 6-asset DD-budget number needs ~$600k of equity for $1m of gross, and the BTC+ETH row that actually authorises anything needs ~$1.38m. No diversification result removes the capital requirement; it cuts it ~40%.",
  "SHOULD THE DEPTH GATE BE A STANDING RAIL? It is unstable: re-sampled 6 times, LTC passed 5/6, LINK 4/6 and SUI 2/6 at a $125k probe. At $1m equal-weighted, LTC's per-asset share is 37.6% of its visible ask ladder. Any multi-asset book needs a live depth precondition per asset per entry, which does not exist today."
